      "deploy_target": "cloud-run",
      "selection_rationale": {
        "runtime": "agent-runtime (Claude Agent SDK) retained as the default — no department framework mandate appears in the intake or clarifications, so neither agent-runtime-langgraph nor agent-runtime-adk is warranted. All five agents (R-004) are roster entries on the one runtime.",
        "pack_basis": "Started from pack-intake-triage (persistence-core, agent-runtime, chat-shell, email-ingest, forms-engine, agent-router, assignment, sla-timers, state-machine, slack-notify, audit-log) — the closest shape match: form intake, agent classification, queue routing, SLA, explicit state machine. Kept forms-engine, agent-router, assignment, sla-timers, state-machine, audit-log and the substrate.",
        "pack_removals": [
          "email-ingest — intake is relationship-manager submission through the app (R-001, R-048); no forward-to-app channel appears in any requirement.",
          "slack-notify — no requirement mentions Slack or any external channel; SLA surfacing is an in-app dashboard (R-034, GAP-001)."
        ],
        "notable_exclusions": [
          "doc-extract / table-extract / ocr-bridge — GAP-004 answered 'structured_input': the extraction stage operates on structured/typed financial input with documents attached for reference only (R-070). Parsing real PDFs/scans is explicitly out of scope, so the entire document-parsing chain is dead weight. This is the single largest build-budget saving in the selection.",
          "sso-oidc — GAP-001 answered 'local': the app owns local user accounts and role assignment (R-067), so auth-basic + rbac + permissions-ui cover identity without an external IdP.",
          "soft-delete / data-retention — the audit trail is append-only with no delete path exposed (R-050); no retention or purge requirement was stated.",
          "cost-meter / request-metrics — R-056's token-usage and latency fields are recorded on the agent-invocation record in transcript-store; a separate spend meter is not demanded.",
          "admin-console / feature-flags — policy and rubric config (R-044, R-045) are versioned data seeded with documented defaults, not a flagged-rollout surface.",
          "export-csv / charting / pdf-render / email-send / scheduling / rate-limit — no requirement demands data export, charts, PDF artifacts, outbound mail, cron jobs, or throttling."
        ],
        "budget_effect": "40 certified modules carry the substrate, identity, audit, workflow, approval, grounding, and Cloud Run readiness layers. The build slices are left with genuinely app-specific work: the deterministic ratio/grading module (R-016 to R-019, R-061), the eight-stage underwriting transition table, the spread template schema, the lending-policy ruleset, and the five agent mandates."
      },
